{"name":"Red Sandstorm","hex":"#e5cac0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"sandstorm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A strong wind carrying clouds of sand and dust through the air."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandstorm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dust storm","blocks":[{"text":"A dust storm, also called a sandstorm, is a meteorological phenomenon common in arid and semi-arid regions. Dust storms arise when a gust front or other strong wind blows loose sand and dirt from a dry surface. Fine particles are transported by saltation and suspension, a process that moves soil from one place and deposits it in another. These storms can reduce visibility, disrupt transportation, and pose serious health risks. Over time, repeated dust storms can reduce agricultural productivity and contribute to desertification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Sandsturm_in_der_Namib_%282017%29.jpg/330px-Sandsturm_in_der_Namib_%282017%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dust_storm","wikidata":"Q182878"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Global_movement_of_dust_from_an_Asian_dust_storm_animation.gif/500px-Global_movement_of_dust_from_an_Asian_dust_storm_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Global_movement_of_dust_from_an_Asian_dust_storm_animation.gif/500px-Global_movement_of_dust_from_an_Asian_dust_storm_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animation showing the global movement of dust from an Asian dust storm.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlobal_movement_of_dust_from_an_Asian_dust_storm_animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg/500px-A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg/1280px-A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg/500px-A_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dust storm in Sahara, painted by George Francis Lyon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Sand_Wind_on_the_Desert.jpg"},{"srcset":"ht